        "original_id": "0a8d9b97-387d-57d0-986a-23e24cb5e141",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: British Airways, BA CityFlyer, Sun Air, Comair, KLM, Kenya Airways, Z-CARD\n- Places: OR Tambo International Airport, Johannesburg, Cape Town International Airport, King Shaka International Airport\n- People: George McDonald\n- Concepts: British Airways franchise destinations, airline ownership stakes, registered trademarks\n\nFacts:\n- Comair operates as a British Airways franchise carrier alongside BA CityFlyer and Sun Air.\n- British Airways franchise carriers Sun Air and Comair operate aircraft in full British Airways livery, offer full British Airways service, and have staff who wear British Airways uniforms.\n- Comair’s main base is OR Tambo International Airport in Johannesburg, and its focus cities are Cape Town International Airport and King Shaka International Airport.\n- KLM has a 26% stake in Kenya Airways.\n- British Airways has an 18% stake in Comair.\n- Z-CARD is a registered trademark for a foldable invented by George McDonald while he was a travel writer and consultant for British Airways.",
